preConditionHook:
// EL: avgRange = Average(high[1] - low[1], rangeLookback) -- the mean bar range
// over the rangeLookback bars ENDING ONE BAR AGO, the window that produced the
// spike bar rather than one that includes the weak follow-through bar being
// judged. The shifted series argument makes Summation read bars 1..rangeLookback.
// Average recomputes from scratch every bar (EL_Summation_Probe, 2,808/2,808)
// and high - low is a price expression with real history, so this is a fresh
// loop over price -- NOT the WFSafe_AvgTrueRange rolling accumulator and not a
// mirrored variable buffer. Summed newest-first, EL's Summation order.
// The weak test uses the SIGNED body (close - open), not its absolute value:
// a bar that closes against the trade is weak whatever its size, which is what
// the source means. Products, not quotients -- EL raises a runtime
// divide-by-zero and a bar whose high equals its low is legal data.
avgRange = 0.0;
for (int i = 1; i <= (int)rangeLookback; ++i) {
    avgRange += high[i] - low[i];
}
avgRange /= (int)rangeLookback;
